# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

config ETH_VRETENO
	bool "Vreteno Ethernet port"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_HDLFACTORY_VRETENO_ETH_ENABLED
	depends on NETWORKING
	select ETH_DRIVER
	help
	  The Ethernet port of the Vreteno machine: two slots each way
	  with a whole frame in each, and ten registers in front of
	  them.

	  `ETH_DRIVER` is what the networking subsystem counts, and a
	  driver that does not select it is a driver the stack never
	  looks for. The serial port made the same mistake with
	  `SERIAL_HAS_DRIVER`, where the symptom was a console that was
	  silently not a console; here it would be an interface that
	  never appears.

	  The dependency on `NETWORKING` is not decoration. `ETH_DRIVER`
	  itself depends on it, so a build without a network stack, which
	  is every build of `hello_world`, refuses the configuration
	  outright rather than quietly building a driver nothing can use.
	  That is what the hermetic build of issue 390 found the first
	  time it compiled this file.

	  Frames are copied into the slots rather than handed over,
	  because Zephyr's `net_pkt` is a chain of fragments and both
	  `net_pkt_read` and `net_pkt_write` linearise. That is why the
	  hardware needs no scatter-gather.
